//0.9.10 v2.4 canary: a class carrying two same-named member methods
//that differ only in staticness. Per NCU v2.4 the staticness flag is
//part of the linkage identity, so the static and instance overloads
//resolve to distinct slots across the .ncu wire.
//
//Pins the bug2 scenario (temp/p31/bug2/): a cross-module instance
//method call that "returns the wrong value." The root cause was never
//a resolution bug — the instance overload resolved correctly and
//returned 999 — but bash/POSIX `$?` truncates the full 32-bit exit
//code to its low 8 bits (999 mod 256 == 231), so the value *looked*
//wrong. The expected value is pinned at 42 (<= 255) so the assertion
//is unambiguous under any shell; see memory nlang-exit-code-limit.
//
//The external-stub path does not support calling an imported class's
//instance method directly (`m.f()` in the consumer); instance access
//happens inside lib via the imported free function callF. See the
//known-limitations entry on cross-module instance access (0.9.11 O2).
class Mix {
	public static int f(int x) {
		return x * 1001;
	}
	public int f() {
		return 42;
	}
	public Mix() {
	}
}
int callF(Mix m) {
	return m.f();
}
